.claude/plans/PLAN-179/staged-w01/.claude/settings.json:759:  "_model_pin_comment": "PLAN-163 T1.1 contingency (ADR-181 §Contingency) — session-default pin. CC 2.1.220 honors the top-level settings key \"model\" (zod: E.string().optional(); describe \"Override the default model used by Claude Code\"; source at 2.1.220 binary offset 226819212, sha256 8addc857..., positioned between \"permissions\" and \"fallbackModel\" in the settings schema — NOT the internal workflow prop \"defaultModel\", NOT the env var ANTHROPIC_MODEL). Pinned to claude-opus-5 (OQ1=b primary/fallback). Rationale: APPENDING claude-sonnet-5 to availableModels makes the 2.1.220 tier-default (sonnet-5) an ALLOWED model, so enforceAvailableModels no longer redirects the session away from it and the session default would silently FLIP from claude-opus-4-8 (=availableModels[0], the prior fallback target) to sonnet-5; the explicit pin forecloses that flip. The pinned value MUST remain a member of availableModels below or enforceAvailableModels rejects it (claude-opus-5 is present). Env ANTHROPIC_MODEL / CLI --model still override per-session at runtime. Mirror this key in templates/settings/settings.base.json or test_session_default_pin reddens.",
.claude/plans/PLAN-179/staged-w01/.claude/settings.json:761:  "availableModels": [
.claude/plans/PLAN-179/staged-w01/.claude/settings.json:763:    "claude-fable-5",
.claude/plans/PLAN-179/staged-w01/.claude/settings.json:769:  "_enforce_available_models_comment": "PLAN-153 wave-backlog (Anthropic ADOPT sweep 2026-07) — Claude Code >=2.1.202 verified semantics: when true and availableModels is a non-empty array, the DEFAULT model selection is also constrained to the allowlist (if the tier default is not in availableModels, Default resolves to the first allowed entry). Closes Default-model drift when the harness tier default moves ahead of our pinned set. Schema-verified optional boolean, valid in project settings (cascade-trust mode). Caveat straight from the binary: if a MANAGED-POLICY settings source exists but fails to load, the harness refuses cascade-trust mode and model enforcement from user/project settings is DISABLED with a warning — fail-open at harness level; acceptable because the availableModels pins still gate explicit selection.",
