 — EDGE-TRIGGERED context-pressure breadcrumb: the session crossed INTO a new context-usage percent rung. A TRANSITION, never a per-turn sample — the hysteresis gate is `audit_emit.should_emit_context_pressure(used_bucket, state_dir)`, which persists the last rung in the marker `context-pressure-last-bucket` under the gitignored `.claude/state/` and FAILS OPEN (any state I/O error means “emit”: a bookkeeping file may never block or crash a user session, and fail-CLOSED here would silently lose the very signal PLAN-179 exists to measure). Without that gate the rail would append one row per prompt while the session sits in a single rung. Off-enum input never re-arms the marker — a bogus value must not be able to suppress the NEXT real transition. Emitted via `emit_generic` (no public typed wrapper — the `settings_tamper_detected` / compaction-pair precedent). Routes through the dedicated `_scrub_*` branch + `_CONTEXT_PRESSURE_OBSERVED_ALLOWLIST`, NEVER `_EMIT_GENERIC_PASSTHROUGH`. DENIED on the wire: the raw token/byte counts, the exact percentage (a precise figure is a side channel on session size — the rung is the governance signal), the transcript text, the plan PATH text, the prompt body. NO ATLAS technique (governance/observability breadcrumb, not a detection signal). |
SPEC/v1/audit-log.schema.md:502:| `ledger_checkpoint_recorded` (v2.59) | `action`, `session_id`, `project`, `outcome` (str — CLOSED enum: `ledger_updated` / `ledger_missing` / `ledger_absent_from_plan` / `error` / `other`; off-enum COERCED to `other`, never echoed), `plan_id` (str — strict `PLAN-NNN` shape via the shared `_compaction_plan_id_ok` validator, else `unknown`; a path-traversal attempt smuggled through this field is rejected, not echoed), `scope_source` (str — CLOSED enum: `plan_dir` / `plan_ac` / `both` / `other`; how the commit was found to be in scope), `in_scope_path_count` (int 0..99 — clamped), `ledger_size_bucket_kib` (int 0..99 — clamped KiB bucket; the unit is in the field NAME), `over_ceiling` (int 0/1), `unverified_ac_claim_count` (int 0..99 — ledger bullets naming an AC/US id with no `verifier:` clause), `commits_since_last_observation` (int 0..99 — clamped), `state_kind` (str — CLOSED enum: `fresh` / `resumed` / `unavailable`; off-enum COERCED to `unavailable`), `would_block` (int 0/1 — what the FUTURE enforce flip WOULD have done; the hook has no deny path today), `event_schema`, `ts`, plus baseline `tokens_*`/`hmac`/`hmac_error`. PLAN-179 W2 US6 / ADR-195 — the work-boundary ledger checkpoint, ADVISORY by construction (`check_ledger_checkpoint.py`, PreToolUse/Bash; no branch in that module returns `permissionDecision`). EVERY int is TYPE-strict: `bool` is rejected as an `int` subclass and a `float` becomes `0` rather than being rounded, because `_lib/canonical_json.py` refuses floats in HMAC-covered fields and the spool writer would drop the ENTIRE event to an `audit-log.errors` breadcrumb (S181 / ADR-055-AMEND-2). Routes through the dedicated `_scrub_*` branch + `_LEDGER_CHECKPOINT_RECORDED_ALLOWLIST`, NEVER `_EMIT_GENERIC_PASSTHROUGH`. DENIED on the wire: the commit MESSAGE, the committed PATHS, the ledger CONTENT, the repo root, any AC text. NO ATLAS technique (governance breadcrumb, not a detection signal). |
SPEC/v1/audit-log.schema.md:503:| `ledger_checkpoint_skipped` (v2.59) | `action`, `session_id`, `project`, `reason` (str — CLOSED enum: `out_of_scope_paths` / `kill_switch` / `hotfix` / `exploratory` / `operator_opt_out` / `unparseable` / `budget_exhausted` / `no_repo` / `other`; off-enum COERCED to `other`, never echoed — the reason is an ENUM and never free text, so "why the rail stayed quiet" is countable without ever describing the commit), `plan_id` (str — strict `PLAN-NNN`, else `unknown`), `commits_since_last_observation` (int 0..99 — clamped), `state_kind` (str — CLOSED enum: `fresh` / `resumed` / `unavailable`), `would_block` (int 0/1 — always `0` on this row: a skip is never a would-block), `event_schema`, `ts`, plus baseline `tokens_*`/`hmac`/`hmac_error`. PLAN-179 W2 US6 / ADR-195 — the same rail's NEGATIVE case, a separate action on purpose: the measure-first window needs a DENOMINATOR, and "skipped because the commit touched no plan-scoped path" and "never observed at all" are different facts that absence alone cannot distinguish. `reason=kill_switch` is emitted even when `CEO_LEDGER_CHECKPOINT=0`, so "the rail is off" is itself measured; `CEO_SOTA_DISABLE=1` is the one fully silent posture (master precedence, CLAUDE.md §4). Same TYPE-strict int discipline as the row above. Routes through the dedicated `_scrub_*` branch + `_LEDGER_CHECKPOINT_SKIPPED_ALLOWLIST`, NEVER `_EMIT_GENERIC_PASSTHROUGH`. NO ATLAS technique. |
