    91	#   `python3 -m pytest --collect-only -q .claude/`   -> 14310 tests, 22 errors
    92	#   The first is the DOCUMENTED scope: pytest.ini `testpaths` is the single
    93	#   source of truth for collection and `make test-collect` runs exactly that
    94	#   invocation — which is also the command every watched doc tells the reader
    95	#   to run. The second (the pre-PLAN-166 derivation) walks `.claude/`
    96	#   directly, which drags in `.claude/sidecars/**` (hypothesis/lightrag
    97	#   probes that need third-party imports) and therefore reports 22 collection
    98	#   ERRORS plus 47 extra cases the reader can never reproduce. Deriving from
    99	#   the wrong population makes the gate reject a truthful doc or accept a
   100	#   stale one, so the derivation is pinned to the documented scope.
   101	#
   102	# NON-INVENTORY NUMERALS (registered omission, not silence): this gate governs
   103	# FRAMEWORK-INVENTORY COUNTS — things you can count in the tree. Latencies
   104	# ("~0.3-1.0s"), prices ("$30-50"), coverage thresholds ("Tier-1 >= 86%"),
   105	# per-profile skill caps and reading times are NOT inventory counts and are
   106	# deliberately outside the contract; they are governed by the artifacts that
   107	# set them (coverage.yml, the profile config), not by a doc-count gate.
   108	# Guard against that exemption becoming a hiding place: the UNMATCHED-APPROX
   109	# SWEEP below fails the gate (a VIOLATION, not a warning) on any
   110	# thousands-shaped approximation ("~N,NNN", "~N.NNN", "~Nk") in a watched doc
   111	# that NO approx rule consumed, naming the doc and the numeral. It MUST be a
   112	# violation: the automated callers (validate.yml runs --quiet, the release
   113	# preflight discards all output) can only observe the exit code, so an
   114	# advisory sweep is a census nobody reads — a new doc numeral with no matcher
   115	# would ship silently, which is exactly the F5 drift class this gate exists
   116	# to stop (PLAN-166 W0 re-pass).
   117	#
   118	# PENDING SITES (registered exemption, never silence). `APPROX_PENDING` below
   119	# can downgrade ONE (doc, metric, EXACT-frozen-value) triple from violation to
   120	# a printed PENDING line. The mechanism exists for mid-session freezes of
   121	# Gate-1 cache-stable files (CLAUDE.md §0), where a re-statement must land at
   122	# a closeout rather than mid-flight; a pending site is also excluded from the
   123	# cross-doc equality pool so the frozen value cannot drag other docs down.
   124	# The registry is EMPTY today: its one historical entry (CLAUDE.md
   125	# tests=13000, frozen during the PLAN-166 W0 session) was CONSUMED when
   126	# commit 65daff0 restated CLAUDE.md to "~14,000 parametrized cases" — and
   127	# keeping the entry past the restatement would have permanently grandfathered
   128	# the exact stale value (a revert to "~13,000" exited 0, because the pending
   129	# lookup runs BEFORE the band check; found by the W0 adversarial re-pass).
   130	# Rules for any future entry:
   131	#   - key on doc + metric + the EXACT frozen value; any OTHER out-of-band
   132	#     figure at the site stays a hard violation;
   133	#   - DELETE the entry in the same commit that lands the restatement — the
   134	#     exemption is not self-clearing against reverts of that restatement;
   135	#   - it prints on every single run, so it cannot rot unnoticed.
   136	#
   137	# NOTE on the two glob-ambiguous / underivable numbers (code-reviewer P2):
   138	#   - "_lib modules" is pinned to the TOP-LEVEL `_lib/*.py` glob (68). The
   139	#     recursive `_lib/**/*.py` count (incl. adapters/ + subdirs) is larger
   140	#     (~140); docs must state the top-level number to match this gate.
   141	#   - "registered hooks" (46) = distinct `*.py` script basenames appearing in
   142	#     command strings of the settings.json hooks{} SUBTREE, parsed as JSON
   143	#     (matches the hook_live_smoke check). S287: the old whole-file grep with
   144	#     a hyphenless regex captured the statusLine `statusline-ceo.py` as a
   145	#     phantom `ceo.py` (47). This is distinct from "hook .py files on disk"
   146	#     (57) — some on-disk hooks are not wired into settings.json — and from
   147	#     "registrations" (48): total hook ENTRIES incl. non-.py commands (one
   148	#     script can fire on several events).
   149	#
   150	# RULE-LIVENESS CONTRACT (S287 vacuous-gate lesson): a metric whose regexes
   151	# match ZERO watched docs reports "no drift" with a number nobody checks —
   152	# a dead gate. The per-metric match count is exported as `rule_matches` in
   153	# --json, and the real-repo test suite asserts every doc-gated metric
   154	# matches >=1 site (test_verify_counts.py). Synthetic test trees are exempt
   155	# by construction (the assertion lives in the real-repo test, not here).
   156	# The historical "6 core hooks" enumeration in CLAUDE.md is a labelled
   157	# historical subset, NOT a live total — it is not gated here.
   158	# ============================================================================
   159	#
   160	# Bash 3.2 portable (macOS default). Doc-parsing delegated to a stdlib-only
   161	# python3 block (python3 is already required for the test-collect step).
   162	
   163	set -euo pipefail
   164	
   165	REPO_ROOT="${VERIFY_COUNTS_ROOT:-$(cd "$(dirname "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")/../../.." && pwd)}"
   166	
   167	QUIET=0
   168	JSON=0
   169	NO_TESTS=0
   170	for arg in "$@"; do
   171	  case "$arg" in
   172	    --quiet)    QUIET=1 ;;
   173	    --json)     JSON=1 ;;
   174	    --no-tests) NO_TESTS=1 ;;
   175	    -h|--help)
   176	      # Usage + the full COUNT/APPROX contract. Keep this range in sync with
   177	      # the header: it ends at the line before "NOTE on the two
   178	      # glob-ambiguous" (S294 — the old '2,75p' truncated mid-sentence once
   179	      # the APPROX CONTRACT block landed).
   180	      sed -n "2,$(( $(grep -n '^# NOTE on the two glob-ambiguous' "$0" | head -1 | cut -d: -f1) - 1 ))p" "$0"
   181	      exit 0
   182	      ;;
   183	    *)
   184	      echo "verify-counts.sh: unknown arg: $arg" >&2
   185	      exit 2
   186	      ;;
   187	  esac
   188	done
   189	
   190	# -------------------------- derive canonical counts -------------------------
   191	
   192	DERIVED_SKILLS=$(find "$REPO_ROOT/.claude/skills" -name SKILL.md 2>/dev/null | wc -l | tr -d ' ')
   193	DERIVED_CORE=$(find "$REPO_ROOT/.claude/skills/core" -name SKILL.md 2>/dev/null | wc -l | tr -d ' ')
   194	DERIVED_FRONTEND=$(find "$REPO_ROOT/.claude/skills/frontend" -name SKILL.md 2>/dev/null | wc -l | tr -d ' ')
   195	DERIVED_DOMAIN=$(find "$REPO_ROOT/.claude/skills/domains" -name SKILL.md 2>/dev/null | wc -l | tr -d ' ')
   196	DERIVED_ADRS=$(ls "$REPO_ROOT"/.claude/adr/ADR-*.md 2>/dev/null | wc -l | tr -d ' ')
   197	DERIVED_HOOK_PY=$(ls "$REPO_ROOT"/.claude/hooks/*.py 2>/dev/null | wc -l | tr -d ' ')
   198	# "_lib modules" = importable application modules, which EXCLUDES the
   199	# package marker __init__.py (the docs cite "68 modules, excluding the
   200	# package __init__.py"; the raw glob is 69 incl. __init__.py). Aligns the
   201	# live count to the documented contract (header note: exact 68).
   202	DERIVED_LIB=$( { find "$REPO_ROOT/.claude/hooks/_lib" -maxdepth 1 -name '*.py' ! -name '__init__.py' 2>/dev/null || true; } | wc -l | tr -d ' ')
   203	# Recursive _lib count (E9-F10 i): find descends adapters/ + subdirs. Guard the
   204	# pipeline against set -e/pipefail when the tree has zero matches.
   205	DERIVED_LIB_RECURSIVE=$(
   206	  { find "$REPO_ROOT/.claude/hooks/_lib" -name '*.py' 2>/dev/null || true; } \
   207	    | wc -l | tr -d ' '
   208	)
   209	# Live SPEC VERSION (E9-F10 iii): single source of truth = the VERSION file.
   210	# Trim whitespace/newlines so the string compares cleanly against doc literals.
   211	DERIVED_VERSION=$(tr -d ' \t\n\r' < "$REPO_ROOT/VERSION" 2>/dev/null || true)
   212	DERIVED_SPEC_V1=$(ls "$REPO_ROOT"/SPEC/v1/*.md 2>/dev/null | wc -l | tr -d ' ')
   213	# "schema files" = the *.schema.md subset (excludes README/compat/cli/shim docs).
   214	# Use find (not ls glob) so a zero-match tree does not trip set -e/pipefail.
   215	DERIVED_SCHEMA_FILES=$(find "$REPO_ROOT/SPEC/v1" -maxdepth 1 -name '*.schema.md' 2>/dev/null | wc -l | tr -d ' ')
   216	# Registered hooks (46) + registrations (48) — parsed from the settings.json
   217	# hooks{} SUBTREE as JSON, never a whole-file grep (S287: the old grep +
   218	# hyphenless regex counted the statusLine `statusline-ceo.py` as a phantom
   219	# `ceo.py`). registered = distinct *.py basenames across hook command
   220	# strings (hyphens admitted); registrations = total hook entries (incl.
   221	# non-.py commands). Unparseable settings.json derives 0/0 (a synthetic
   222	# tree citing non-zero then fails loud — fail-closed on input).
   223	_reg_out=$(python3 - "$REPO_ROOT/.claude/settings.json" <<'PYREG' 2>/dev/null
   224	import json, os, re, sys
   225	try:
   226	    s = json.load(open(sys.argv[1], encoding="utf-8"))
   227	except Exception:
   228	    print("0 0"); raise SystemExit(0)
   229	hooks = s.get("hooks", {})
   230	distinct, total = set(), 0
   231	if isinstance(hooks, dict):
   232	    for _event, matchers in hooks.items():
   233	        if not isinstance(matchers, list):
   234	            continue
   235	        for m in matchers:
   236	            if not isinstance(m, dict):
   237	                continue
   238	            for h in m.get("hooks", []):
   239	                if not isinstance(h, dict):
   240	                    continue
   241	                total += 1
   242	                for tok in re.findall(r"[A-Za-z0-9_.-]+\.py", str(h.get("command", ""))):
   243	                    distinct.add(os.path.basename(tok))
   244	print("%d %d" % (len(distinct), total))
   245	PYREG
   246	) || _reg_out="0 0"
   247	DERIVED_REGISTERED=${_reg_out% *}
   248	DERIVED_REGISTRATIONS=${_reg_out#* }
   249	
   250	# Test count: collect-only over the DOCUMENTED scope — no path argument, so
   251	# pytest.ini `testpaths` decides, which is byte-for-byte what `make
   252	# test-collect` runs and what every watched doc tells the reader to run.
   253	# The previous derivation passed `.claude/` explicitly; that walks
   254	# `.claude/sidecars/**` too and reports COLLECTION ERRORS plus phantom
   255	# cases the reader can never reproduce — a different population from the
   256	# one the docs cite. The single dated measurement of BOTH populations
   257	# lives in the COLLECTION SCOPE header block above; do not paste a second
   258	# pair here (W0 re-pass round 2: an undated pair in this comment drifted
