    48	## What's in the box
    49	
    50	All counts below are verifiable from a clean checkout (see *Verifying the numbers*).
    51	
    52	| Component | Count | Notes |
    53	|---|---|---|
    54	| Skill checklists | **166** | 42 core + 8 frontend + 116 domain |
    55	| Hook scripts (on disk) | **59** | Python entrypoints under `.claude/hooks/` |
    56	| Hooks wired in `settings.json` | **48** | distinct scripts, 50 event registrations |
    57	| Shared library modules | **71** | stdlib-only, under `.claude/hooks/_lib/` (excluding the package `__init__.py`) |
    58	| Slash commands | **27** | under `.claude/commands/` |
    59	| Architecture decision records | **198** | under `.claude/adr/` |
    60	| Tests | **~15,400 cases** | reported by `pytest --collect-only` across the hook, script, and conformance suites |
    61	
    62	The gap between **59 hook scripts** on disk and **48 wired** is benign: several non-event modules are activated through in-process dispatch (invoked by other hooks) rather than by a direct `settings.json` event registration.
    63	
    64	**Runtime dependencies: none.** Hooks and scripts are Python ≥ 3.9, **standard library only** — zero third-party runtime packages. See [`SBOM.md`](SBOM.md). (Development and CI use third-party test tooling such as pytest; the installed runtime does not.)
    65	
    66	There is also a **published compliance contract** under `SPEC/v1/` (32 files — 28 `*.schema.md` plus contract docs, version-pinned), a TLA+ specification of the core circuit-breaker state machine, a conformance harness, and a local read-only audit dashboard.
