   247	
   248	Two new hooks, both **advisory, both fail-open, neither blocks a tool
   249	call today**:
   250	
   251	- **`check_compact_pinning.py`** (`SessionStart`, matcher `compact`):
   252	  after a context compaction, re-states the pinned governance
   253	  constraints from a CODE constant (`_lib/pinned_constraints.py`) via
   254	  `additionalContext`, so the summarizer cannot evict them. Kill switch:
   255	  `CEO_CONSTRAINT_PINNING=0`.
   256	- **`check_ledger_checkpoint.py`** (`PreToolUse`, matcher `Bash`): on the
   257	  FIRST `git commit` of a Bash call (staging done in earlier tool calls)
   258	  that lands plan-scoped work, reports whether that plan's `LEDGER.md` is
   259	  in the same commit. Scope is derived MECHANICALLY from the paths staged
   260	  (and, under `-a`, the tracked modifications present) at the moment the
   261	  hook fires, BEFORE the command runs: `git add x && git commit` on a
   262	  clean index is `skipped`, a mutation made earlier in the same call is
   263	  not seen, and a second commit in the same call is not inspected (signed
   264	  condition 77 of rc.1). No branch in the module returns a decision —
   265	  there is no deny arm to disarm. Kill switches:
   266	  `CEO_LEDGER_CHECKPOINT=0`, `CEO_SOTA_DISABLE=1` (`b07be9b`, `bc82651`).
   267	- **`session_memory_delta_observed`** at `SessionEnd` records whether the
   268	  project's memory directory saw activity inside this session's time window
   269	  (stat-only: no memory content is read or logged). The directory is shared
   270	  by every session of the project and a stat carries no author, so a
   271	  concurrent session's write counts too: `written` is window activity, never
   272	  proof that THIS session wrote memory. The window opens at the whole second
   273	  after the recorded session start, so a write inside that first second is
   274	  not counted (signed condition 20 of rc.1).
